<title>BELGIUM: EU intervention grain stocks at 1.83 mln T net.</title>
<headline>EU intervention grain stocks at 1.83 mln T net.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union intervention grain stocks fell to 1.83 million tonnes net, from 2.60 million tonnes at the start of the season on July 1, 1996, the European Commission said on Monday.</p>
<p>An additional 528,713 tonnes of grain offered into intervention stores was still being considered, compared with 333,095 tonnes on June 5.</p>
<p>The deadline for intervention offers was May 31, except in Sweden where an extra month is allowed.</p>
<p>European Union intervention grain stocks (tonnes)</p>
<p>			12/6/97	 5/6/97	    1/7/96</p>
<p> All cereals	1,828,578     1,717,104	 2,596,112</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p> Soft wheat	   346,598	 338,494	   458,978</p>
<p> Durum wheat	    nil	     nil		   nil</p>
<p> Barley		 550,238	 475,95	  1,343,870</p>
<p> Rye		    929,367	 900,285	   793,261</p>
<p> Maize		    2,375	   2,375		   3</p>
<p> Sorghum		  nil	     nil		   nil</p>
<p> Triticale		nil	     nil		   nil</p>
<p>NB: Figures are net after deduction of domestic and export sales commitments</p>
